-- title:
--   Integral closedness from a crossing presentation gh=varpi^e w
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring and let $R$ be a noetherian local commutative domain which is a domain and an $O$-algebra. Let $\varpi \in O$ be irreducible, and assume that the composite $O \to R \to R/\mathfrak m_R$ of the structure map with the residue map of $R$ is surjective. Let $g, h, w \in R$ with $w$ a unit, let $e$ be a natural number with $e \ge 1$, and suppose that $gh = \varpi^e w$, where $\varpi$ denotes its image under $O \to R$. Suppose further that the maximal ideal of $R$ is the ideal generated by $\varpi$, $g$ and $h$; that the ideals generated by $\{\varpi, g\}$ and by $\{\varpi, h\}$ are both prime; and that $h$ does not lie in the ideal generated by $\{\varpi, g\}$, nor $g$ in the ideal generated by $\{\varpi, h\}$. Then $R$ is integrally closed, i.e. every element of its fraction field that is integral over $R$ lies in the image of $R$.
--
--   This is the local criterion identifying the completed local ring at an ordinary double point of the type $\varpi^e = gh$ (a singularity of type $A_{e-1}$ in the Mazur–Rapoport classification) as normal, with no hypothesis on the residue characteristic, in particular none on the invertibility of $2$. It is used in the analysis of the local rings of modular curves at nodal points, where places centred at the $j$-invariants $0$ and $1728$ and height one primes attached to crossing parameters are extracted from a crossing presentation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_isIntegrallyClosed_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_of_mul_eq_pow_mul_isUnit.lean

